  "facts": [
    "The Thirrë-Kalimash Tunnel, stretching 5,490 meters, was Albania's longest tunnel upon its 2018 opening, a milestone surpassed only by the 5,990‑meter Llogara Tunnel on the SH 8.",
    "By cutting travel time between Tirana and the Kosovo border from eight to three hours, the Thirrë-Kalimash Tunnel has become a vital artery for boosting Kosovan tourism and strengthening cross‑border ties.",
    "In 2018, the first toll booths on Albania’s A1 Highway appeared at the tunnel’s eastern end near Kolsh, charging passenger cars €5 as part of the country’s inaugural toll‑road system."
